From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: clock: mediatek: add MT6897 clock controllers

Add the bindings for the clock controllers of the MediaTek MT6897
(Dimensity 8300) SoC:

- The system clock controllers apmixedsys, topckgen and vlpckgen provide
  the PLLs, dividers and muxes.
- The functional clock controllers pericfg_ao, ufscfg_ao and ufscfg_pdn
  provide clock gates. The two UFS blocks also provide the reset lines of
  the UFS M-PHY, UniPro, crypto engine and host controller.

As on MT8196, some PLLs, muxes and gates are switched through the
hardware voter, which the nodes point to with mediatek,hardware-voter.

The clock identifiers follow the tables of the MediaTek vendor driver
(OnePlus Pad GPL release), without the vendor's one-to-one alias clocks.

---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..60db7997f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: MediaTek Functional Clock Controller for MT6897
+
+maintainers:
+  - buntOS contributors <buntos@localhost>
+
+description: |
+  The clock architecture in MediaTek SoCs is structured like below:
+  PLLs -->
+          dividers -->
+                      muxes
+                           -->
+                              clock gate
+
+  The device nodes provide clock gate control in different IP blocks. The
+  two UFS blocks also provide the reset lines of the UFS M-PHY, UniPro,
+  inline crypto engine and host controller.
+
+  The identifiers of the clocks are in
+  include/dt-bindings/clock/mediatek,mt6897-clock.h and those of the resets
+  in include/dt-bindings/reset/mediatek,mt6897-resets.h.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    items:
+      - enum:
+          - mediatek,mt6897-pericfg-ao
+          - mediatek,mt6897-ufscfg-ao
+          - mediatek,mt6897-ufscfg-pdn
+      - const: syscon
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  '#clock-cells':
+    const: 1
+
+  '#reset-cells':
+    const: 1
+
+  mediatek,hardware-voter:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      Phandle to the hardware voter (HWV) register block. The HWV is a
+      SoC-internal MCU that collects clock votes from the application
+      processor and the remote processors. On MT6897 it opens and closes
+      some of the pericfg_ao gates.
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - '#clock-cells'
+
+allOf:
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          contains:
+            const: mediatek,mt6897-pericfg-ao
+    then:
+      required:
+        - mediatek,hardware-voter
+      properties:
+        '#reset-cells': false
+    else:
+      required:
+        - '#reset-cells'
+      properties:
+        mediatek,hardware-voter: false
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    clock-controller@11036000 {
+        compatible = "mediatek,mt6897-pericfg-ao", "syscon";
+        reg = <0x11036000 0x1000>;
+        mediatek,hardware-voter = <&hwv>;
+        #clock-cells = <1>;
+    };
+  - |
+    clock-controller@112bb000 {
+        compatible = "mediatek,mt6897-ufscfg-pdn", "syscon";
+        reg = <0x112bb000 0x1000>;
+        #clock-cells = <1>;
+        #reset-cells = <1>;
+    };
